is supplied as a set `cl` containing\n`R°`; the boundary is the set-difference `cl ∖ R°`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:computational-boundary","label":"def:computational-boundary","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-boundary.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}